 "content": {
  "text": "Ao 28.4.199\nJudith, It is a shame that I did not\nDear\nwrite you and today only I thank you very\nmuch for your \"Pessach wishes, and I hope\nthat you all, your great family, had a good\ntime together. We had Possach, no Seder, in\nEva's home, altogether 14 people. My duty\nwas to prepare the \"Mazzeknodel\". The only\nperson missing was deborah. Gabriel just\narrived before.\nIn respect of our successors I am not able\nto give you very much information. My\nmother Lotte was the yongest of 3 and\nfather Max W. died before her birth\nher\nalways was very closed to her sisters\nShe\nand brothers. - had a feeling and stop.\n54\ned this letter. And really on 28.4. only\narrived your letter from 15.4.94 Right\nnow I heard on Television, that the peace.\ntreaty was signed today in Egypt with\nClp. And Syria and Jordan? We all hope\nvery much that all the sacrifices will have\nsucess. - It is really impressoning to hear\nof the Bar Mizwah of your sisters son\nat the hotel. I cannot imagine this\ncelebration in the open. I send my best\nwishes for the boy and the whole family\njust wrote the list of our family\nI remember the things. I dont have\nas.\nanything written and made it out of\nI am sorry\nIt is incomplate\nmy memory.",
